title AMUS24 — Constel tenure: a leader holds its title only while a majority answers
prompt continue the recursion — after AMUS23 (transfer) shipped, take the next agent-doable pure crux Lindy-first, self-approve, send as its own signed round
think AMUS20's linearizable read refuses to serve from a deposed leader — but only reactively, when a read is attempted; the matching PROACTIVE guard was missing, so a minority-partition leader could linger believing it leads
think Raft's CheckQuorum (§6.2/§9.6) is that guard and a clean pure rung: a leader counts heartbeat acks each window (counting itself) and steps down when its backing falls below the majority threshold — composes only quorum.majority_of and roster.max_piers
think it is the family companion to AMUS22 (pre-vote keeps a rejoining node from disrupting a healthy leader) and AMUS23 (transfer hands off on purpose); CheckQuorum keeps an isolated leader from lingering, so the sky neither disrupts a good leader nor clings to a stranded one
think named the module tenure.rye — a clean collision-free word (mandate collides with the seated Mandate/MAND vane; heartbeat/confirm already appear as ordinary words); a leader holds tenure only while a majority still answers
obs GREEN on the first build across six blocks; TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0, zero usize; backing bounded to roster.max_piers, still_commands and should_step_down exact inverses about the threshold
obs the crux block splits a five-pier sky 2|3 — the stranded old leader (backing 2 of threshold 3) steps down while the majority side's new leader (backing 3) commands, so a ghost leader never shadows the sky
loom witness=amus_tenure_witness blocks=6 result=GREEN build=first-try usize=0
